creased. When the distribution of DNA damage in the
liver cells was analyzed (Fig. 2), cells in the treated populations exhibited % tail DNAs of up to 71.1% (and OTMs
of up to 18.3, not shown). With blood lymphocytes, %
tail DNA from the treated animals was no higher than
